  <section class="section" id="general" style="padding-top: 40px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);">General</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin: 4px 0 0;">General questions about the platform.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What is Teamwork Commerce?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is a global, AI-enabled retail platform that natively integrates enterprise POS, OMS, Inventory Management, RFID, and AI into one system. It powers 30,000+ terminals across 40+ countries with 99.99% uptime, serving mid-market and enterprise retailers in fashion, footwear, stadiums, museums, jewelry, and specialty retail.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does Teamwork Commerce handle offline transactions?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Store-and-Forward keeps the POS selling through a network outage. Card data is encrypted at the point of capture, on the payment terminal or Tap to Pay on iPhone, and never stored on the POS. Sales queue locally and sync to the back office automatically when connectivity returns. Offline card acceptance depends on the payment provider you use.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What makes the RFID solution different from competitors?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce offers the industry's only native end-to-end RFID stack, no third-party middleware required. It covers tag encoding at receiving, RFID-enabled checkout (scan an entire basket in one tap), real-time item-level tracking, and full-store cycle counts in minutes. This delivers 99.9% inventory accuracy.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What is the AI at the point of sale?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The AI is built into the point of sale for store associates. Rather than searching a catalog, the associate asks in plain language, by typing or by voice: "warm coat for women" returns the matching stock, then narrows by color or size. Because it reads the same product and customer records the POS is already working from, it can also show what that customer bought before and suggest what to show next. The practical effect is that a new associate can answer the questions only your most experienced staff could answer before, on the floor and in front of the customer, instead of losing the sale to "let me go and check". It runs at the point of sale, and it is part of the platform rather than a separate product to buy or integrate.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Is Teamwork Commerce SOC 2 compliant?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce holds SOC 2 Type 2, and is GDPR and PCI DSS compliant. SOC 2 coverage for a given deployment is confirmed as part of your agreement. The platform also supports fiscal compliance standards including NF525 (France) and TSE (Germany) across 40+ countries.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How long does deployment take?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Implementations typically run from around 120 days to two years, depending on fleet size, operational complexity, and how many integrations are in scope. Our own service team leads every implementation, working alongside any systems integrator or technology partner you bring. Once a retailer is live, opening an additional store is a matter of hours rather than a project.</p></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

